#!spectest
# mode: run
# adjudicator: ggdef
# since: spec-v0.1
# features: [move, lazy-bind, emove]
# doc: |
#   The EMove witness (RFC §6(c) adjudication #3; devbook/11:716-733). `s` is
#   bound from the PRE-move name `v`; the vector is then moved to `w` and
#   mutated through `w` — a name asymmetry (bind keyed by `v`, mutation via
#   `w`) that is the essence of the EMove phenomenon. Under value semantics
#   (D1) `s` holds the bind-time snapshot, so the PRE-mutation value `hello`
#   prints. Production converged on this after its Expr::Move read-through bug
#   was fixed (B1 finding).
# expect:
#   exit: 0
#   stdout: "hello\n"
#!end

void main():
    Vector[String] v = ["hello", "world"]
    String s = v.get(0).unwrap()
    Vector[String] w = !v
    w.set(0, "mutated")
    print(s)
